From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hans2294 <22217531+hans2294@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:41:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan_haiku.h: Haiku window surfaces through
 VK_EXT_headless_surface

A local structure, chained into VkHeadlessSurfaceCreateInfoEXT, carries
the BView a driver presents into; its type lies in an unassigned block.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/vulkan/vulkan_haiku.h | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/vulkan/vulkan_haiku.h

diff --git a/include/vulkan/vulkan_haiku.h b/include/vulkan/vulkan_haiku.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..30e9db6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/vulkan/vulkan_haiku.h
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+#ifndef VULKAN_HAIKU_H_
+#define VULKAN_HAIKU_H_ 1
+
+/*
+** Copyright 2026, hans2294.
+** Distributed under the terms of the MIT License.
+*/
+
+/*
+ * Vulkan surfaces in Haiku windows, ahead of a registered extension: chain a
+ * VkHaikuViewSurfaceCreateInfoHAIKU into the VkHeadlessSurfaceCreateInfoEXT
+ * of vkCreateHeadlessSurfaceEXT (VK_EXT_headless_surface). A driver that
+ * knows the structure presents into the BView, and the swapchain extent
+ * follows the view's bounds; others ignore it and make a headless surface.
+ *
+ * The structure type is not one Khronos handed out (it lies in the block
+ * of extension number 1000); it is local to this Haiku port.
+ */
+
+#include "vulkan_core.h"
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+#define VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_HAIKU_VIEW_SURFACE_CREATE_INFO_HAIKU \
+    ((VkStructureType)1000999000)
+
+typedef struct VkHaikuViewSurfaceCreateInfoHAIKU {
+    VkStructureType    sType;
+    const void*        pNext;
+    void*              view;    /* a BView* in a window; must outlive the surface */
+} VkHaikuViewSurfaceCreateInfoHAIKU;
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif
